  message: "FILED EVIDENCE REFUTED on the item own repro, using the preserved before/after cohort arms rather than re-reasoning. All THREE supposedly-lost kserve flows carry source_primitive=run, and pythons only two run SOURCES are flask.Flask.run and uvicorn.run - so a local def run(cmd) in a helm-version script was matched by name to a Flask web-server entrypoint and declared a source of untrusted input. That is a WI-damir false positive, not a loss. The SINK side was never broken, which is the half the filing had backwards: the edge run -> python:subprocess:0-0:run:external_symbol exists and still matches subprocess.run today, so the wrapper is already in sink_callers and propagation never needed to traverse the wrapper body. Both proposed fixes (transitive closure; thin-wrapper propagation) targeted a sink-side problem that does not exist. No real flow is possible there at all: subprocess appears ZERO times in pythons 83 catalogued sources. What survives is the SOURCE-side wrapper gap - source_callers is forward-scanned and the BFS runs forward, so a first-party function that calls a source and RETURNS it makes only itself a source caller while its callers, which receive the tainted value, are upstream and never visited (reverse_adj at taint.py:1409 is built and read by nobody). That gap has ZERO measured instances and cannot be demonstrated on this repro. Lowered to P3 and a new repro is required before any fix, because filing a fix shape on an unmeasured thesis is this items own error."  # c28c
